1.29.m:
Sanaka said:
I shall tell the determination of the lunar days and the rule of expiation;
listen to that, O best of sages, by which accomplishment of ritual actions comes to be.

1.31.m:
Givers of food, O best of sages, go while eating delicious [delicacies];
givers of water go happily, drinking excellent milk;
givers of buttermilk and givers of curds obtain their respective enjoyments;
and givers of ghee, givers of honey, and givers of milk, O foremost of the twice-born,

having reached the surface of the earth, they become immovable beings and the like.
Nārada said:
O Lord, an ocean of compassion, a doubt has arisen in my mind;
